verses.text:
This is what Yahweh says:
“For three transgressions of Moab,
yes, for four, I will not turn it back;
because he burned the bones of the king of Edom
to lime.{a}

From among them I will cut off the judge{c}
and slay all her princes along with him,”
says Yahweh.

they who long to grind the heads of the poor into the dust of the ground{e}
and turn aside the way of the humble;
a man and his father go in to the same young woman,
so that my holy name is defiled;

Look, I am going to make you groan where you are,{h}
as a wagon groans
that is loaded with sheaves.

Flight will fail the swift;
the strong will not retain his strength,
nor will the mighty save his life.

The one who handles the bow will not hold firm;
the fleet-footed will not get away,
and the one who rides the horse will not save his life.

“You alone have I known{a}
of all the families of the earth;
therefore I will punish you
for all your iniquities.”

Surely the Lord Yahweh will not do a thing
unless he has disclosed his counsel{c}
to his servants the prophets.

The lion has roared;
who will not fear?
The Lord Yahweh has spoken;
who can but prophesy?

“Come to Bethel, and transgress;
to Gilgal, and multiply transgression;
bring your sacrifices every morning,
your tithes every three days;{d}

“I also held back the rain from you
while there were three months yet until harvest;
on one town I made it rain,
and on another town I made it not rain;
one plot was rained on,
and the plot that got no rain dried up.

“I struck you with scorching and mildew;
the locust ate your gardens and your vineyards,
your figs and your olives, many as they were;
but you have not come back to me,”
declares Yahweh.

“I sent pestilence on you in the way of Egypt;
with the sword I slew your young men,
and your horses were taken captive,
and I made the stink of your camps go up even into your nostrils;
but you have not come back to me,”
declares Yahweh.

“Therefore this is what I will do to you, Israel;
because I will do this to you,
prepare to meet your God, Israel!”

Do not go seeking Bethel;
do not enter Gilgal;
do not pass over to Beersheba;
for Gilgal shall go off into exile,{b}
and Bethel shall become nothing.”{c}

Now you shall carry off Sakkuth your king
and Kaiwan, your star god,{j} your idols
that you fashioned for yourselves;

Cross over to Calneh and see;
go from there to Hamath the great;
then go down to Gath of the Philistines.
Are you better than these kingdoms?
Or is their territory greater than your territory?{a}

you who rejoice in Lo-debar,{f}
who say, “Was it not by our own strength
that we took Karnaim for ourselves?”

“In that day,” declares the Lord Yahweh,
“I will bring the sun down at midday
and cover the earth with darkness while it is still day.{e}

Your festivals I will change to grief
and all your singing to dirges;
I will put sackcloth around every waist
and shave every head;
I will make it like mourning for an only son,
and the end of it a bitter day.

I saw the Lord standing beside{a} the altar, and he said:
“Strike the capitals, so that the thresholds shake,
and shatter them on the heads of all of them;
and those who are left of them I will kill with the sword.
Not one of them will flee away;
not one of them will escape.

The Lord Yahweh of Armies{b}—
at his touch the earth melts,
and all its inhabitants mourn;
the whole of it rises like the Nile
and falls back like the river of Egypt;

so that they may possess the remnant of Edom
and all the nations who are called by my name,”{g}
declares Yahweh who does this.

“Look, the days are coming,” declares Yahweh,
“when the plowman will overtake the reaper,
and the treader of grapes him who sows the seed;
the mountains will drip sweet wine,
and all the hills will flow with it.{h}

I will bring back the captivity{i} of my people Israel;
they shall build the wasted cities and dwell in them;
they shall plant vineyards and drink the wine from them,
and lay out gardens and eat the fruit from them.
